@startuml
title OmniDesk AI SDLC Roadmap

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "1. Project Planning" as Planning
rectangle "2. Requirements Engineering" as Requirements
rectangle "3. System Analysis" as Analysis
rectangle "4. System Design" as Design
rectangle "5. Implementation" as Implementation
rectangle "6. Testing" as Testing
rectangle "7. Deployment" as Deployment
rectangle "8. Maintenance" as Maintenance

Planning --> Requirements
Requirements --> Analysis
Analysis --> Design
Design --> Implementation
Implementation --> Testing
Testing --> Deployment
Deployment --> Maintenance

note bottom of Design
Milestones define meaningful outcomes.
Agile Sprints organize iterative
execution across SDLC activities.
end note

note bottom of Planning
Project Definition is an input
to Project Planning and remains
outside the SDLC documentation sequence.
end note

note bottom of Testing
The numbered SDLC activities do not
require strict Waterfall execution.
end note

@enduml
